  "articleBody": "When unexpected damage hits your roof in Texas, you're quickly faced with a big question: repair or replace? It’s a decision that impacts your home’s protection, your wallet, and your peace of mind. Both options have their place, but knowing which one is right for your specific situation requires a careful look at several factors. Discounted Roofing Co. helps homeowners in the DFW area navigate this choice with clear, honest advice.\n\n### Questions to Ask Before You Decide\n\n- **How old is your current roof and what’s its general condition?** A newer roof with localized damage is usually repairable. If your roof is nearing the end of its expected lifespan (often 20-25 years for asphalt shingles), even minor damage might push it into replacement territory. An older roof might have underlying issues that repairs won't fully address.\n- **How extensive and widespread is the damage?** Is it a few missing shingles from a windstorm, or widespread hail damage across multiple slopes? Small, isolated issues typically call for repair. Widespread damage, especially if it compromises the roof's integrity or involves the underlying decking, often warrants a full replacement to ensure long-term durability.\n- **Are compatible roofing materials readily available for repair?** Sometimes, especially with older or specialty roofs, finding an exact match for repair materials can be difficult or impossible. Mismatched materials can affect both aesthetics and performance. A replacement solves this by giving you a fresh start with new, readily available materials.\n- **Will multiple repairs truly fix the problem, or are they just temporary patches?** If you've had recurring leaks in different spots or if repairs seem to fail quickly, it might indicate a more systemic problem. Repeatedly patching a failing roof can end up costing more than a replacement in the long run.\n- **What are the long-term costs and benefits of each option?** Compare the immediate cost of a repair versus the investment in a replacement. Consider the extended lifespan a new roof provides, improved energy efficiency (with newer materials), and enhanced curb appeal. A professional estimate from Discounted Roofing Co. will break down these costs clearly.\n- **Does the damage affect interior components like decking or insulation?** If there’s water damage to the roof decking, attic insulation, or even interior ceilings, a repair might only address the surface. A full replacement allows for a thorough inspection and repair or replacement of these critical underlying components, ensuring your entire roof system is healthy.\n\nDiscounted Roofing Co. emphasizes honest recommendations. We’ll evaluate your roof with a free inspection, providing clear documentation with photos and explaining what we find. Our team will help you understand if repairs can effectively restore your roof’s integrity or if a full replacement offers the best long-term protection and value for your home, especially given Texas's challenging weather. We're committed to guiding you through the process step by step, ensuring you make a confident decision.\n\nReady to get an honest assessment of your roof's needs? Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a free inspection.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
